DECISIONS 213, CODEGEN.md §3.5, §7.9 (log-2026-11-01): a cpp emit whose mode check refused (E8009) reports a name collision only when the plan of every mode gen/cpp writes (baked, data, types) has it: two @cpp(name:) overrides, or a type and an override taking its name, clash in every mode; a let and a const overridden alike do not. Every one of those modes writes the defines, so two equal define names stay E8005.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A.
record A @cpp(name: "W") {
  /// N.
  n: Int
}

/// B.
record B @cpp(name: "W") {
  /// N.
  n: Int
}

/// X.
record X {
  /// N.
  n: Int
}

/// Y.
record Y @cpp(name: "X") {
  /// N.
  n: Int
}

/// An enum.
enum Color { red }

/// Z.
record Z @cpp(name: "Color") {
  /// N.
  n: Int
}

/// One.
@cpp(name: "same")
let one: A = { n: 1 }

/// Two.
@cpp(name: "same")
const TWO = 2

/// First kinds.
enum First @cpp(defines: "K_") {
  /// One.
  one
}

/// Second kinds.
enum Second @cpp(defines: "K_") {
  /// One again.
  one
}

emit cpp { out: "@features/a", namespace: "a", mode: zzmode }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8005]  a/a.canon:10:8
  cpp: W is generated for both a.A and a.B; rename one of them with @cpp(name:)

error[E8005]  a/a.canon:22:8
  cpp: X is generated for both a.X and a.Y; rename one of them with @cpp(name:)

error[E8005]  a/a.canon:31:8
  cpp: Color is generated for both a.Color and a.Z; rename one of them with @cpp(name:)

error[E8005]  a/a.canon:51:6
  #define K_one is written for both a.First.one and a.Second.one; change one prefix, or rename one declaration

error[E8009]  a/a.canon:56:54
  invalid mode zzmode for emit cpp: expected one of baked, embedded, data, types

5 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
